In article <1993Jul3.152227.17808@waikato.ac.nz> drysdall@waikato.ac.nz writes:
>I was just wondering, what is the difference between #invoking and #applying
>something? Obviously, they do different things :)

Incidentally, you might confuse some people presenting the commands as you
have.  You should use #invoke and a)pply.  The reason for this is that the
invoke command is an extended command accessed using the # key, whereas the
apply command is a standard command, accessed by hitting the 'a' key.

In any case, the difference between the #invoke command and the a)pply
command is simple.  Standard magic and non-magical items are used via
the a)pply command.  This includes things like blindfolds, stethescopes,
musical instruments, etc.  The special powers of artifacts must be
#invoked.  At this point only the various quest artifacts have any powers
that can be invoked.  For more details, see the Artifacts section in 
the WCST Spoiler Segment that just got released.

